# ENGINE-UNIVERSAL-SERVICES.17 slice 4 — G1: `g0_unguarded.ebnf` plus a BYTE-SET follow guard.
#
# ⛔ ONE-DIFFERENCE CONTROL. Byte-for-byte `g0_unguarded.ebnf` except for the `prim` line and the
# `residual_first_byte` rule it needs. Nothing else may differ, or the comparison is not a control.
#
#   G0:  prim := prim_base ( prim_suffix )*
#   G1:  prim := prim_base ( prim_suffix &residual_first_byte )*
#
# WHAT IT MODELS. Slice 2's option (iii) in its CHEAP form — `X_lr_base ( X_lr_suffix &FIRST(residual) )*`
# with `FIRST(residual)` compiled to a one-byte test. The holder's residual is
# `tick lparen lit rparen`; `tick := trivia "'"` and `trivia` is nullable, so FIRST(residual) is
# `{ ' , / }` — the tick itself, plus `/` contributed by the nullable comment rule that leads it.
# That is the shipped over-approximation, reproduced here rather than asserted: slice 2 measured
# `~` (over-approximated) on 157 of 157 sites across both SystemVerilog grammars.
#
# ⭐ THIS IS THE CHARITABLE FORM OF THE BYTE TEST, DELIBERATELY. The emitted Q-GUARD reads
# `parser.input.as_bytes()[parser.position]` with no layout skip at all
# (`ast_based_generator.rs:6014-6020`), so a real byte guard also mis-fires on plain WHITESPACE at
# the boundary. Writing it here as a lookahead over a regex lets the engine's layout skipper run
# first, which strictly HELPS G1. The finding is therefore a lower bound on the cheap form's
# failure: even given free whitespace handling, it still slips on a comment (case E3).
@entry: true
scratch := kw_k eq outer_cast semi
outer_cast := ct tick lparen lit rparen
ct := kw | prim
prim := prim_base ( prim_suffix &residual_first_byte )*
prim_base := lit | cast_seed
cast_seed := kw tick lparen lit rparen
prim_suffix := tick lparen lit rparen

# THE GUARD, and the whole of the difference from G0: one byte drawn from FIRST(residual) =
# { ' , / }. The `/` is not a mistake and must not be "tightened" — it is what the shipped FIRST
# machinery computes, because `trivia` is nullable and leads `tick`.
residual_first_byte := /['\/]/

lit := trivia /n/
kw := trivia /t/
kw_k := trivia /k/
eq := trivia "="
semi := trivia ";"
tick := trivia "'"
lparen := trivia "("
rparen := trivia ")"

@branch_policy: priority_first
trivia := (line_comment | block_comment)*
line_comment := /\/\/[^\n]*(\n|$)/
block_comment := /\/\*([^*]|\*+[^*\/])*\*+\//
